-- Boundary module: the Members of Parliament (Staff) Act 1984 (Cth) provisions that s 8(2)(b)
-- of the Diplomatic Appointments (Selection Process) Bill 2026 reads.
-- Source: Members of Parliament (Staff) Act 1984, Compilation No. 9, compilation date
-- 14 March 2026, register ID C2026C00093 (source bundle item cth-mops-act-1984).
-- Reference register: REF-10 (ss 3, 3AA, 4, 11), REF-13 (s 3 'relevant office', s 4).
-- Depth 1: the definitions and the employing power, nothing further (s 12 arrangements and
-- conditions, and the earlier compilations of REF-11, are not encoded).
--
-- Two byte-identical copies of this file exist: mops-1984.l4 in the subject folder, which the Bill's
-- modules import, and boundary/mops-1984.l4, the path the reference register names. The installed l4
-- cannot import from another folder (ENCODING-NOTES.md, E-01).

§ `Positions a parliamentarian or former Prime Minister may occupy`

-- The positions that matter to the MOP(S) Act s 3 and to s 8(2)(b) of the Bill. A person
-- occupying none of the named positions who is a senator or member is "another senator or
-- member". "Minister" here means a Minister of State other than the Prime Minister; the Prime
-- Minister is listed separately because s 8(2)(b)(i) of the Bill names that office.
DECLARE Position IS ONE OF
    `Prime Minister`
    `Minister other than the Prime Minister`
    `Leader of the Opposition in the Senate`
    `Leader of the Opposition in the House of Representatives`
    `Deputy Leader of the Opposition in the Senate`
    `Deputy Leader of the Opposition in the House of Representatives`
    `shadow Minister`
    `leader or deputy leader in a House of a recognized political party`
    `another senator or member`
    `former Prime Minister who is not a parliamentarian`

-- The three kinds of employment under s 11.
DECLARE `MOP(S) Act employment` IS ONE OF
    `electorate employee`
    `personal employee (Ministerial)`
    `personal employee (non-Ministerial)`

§ `Members of Parliament (Staff) Act 1984 s 3 -- Interpretation`

-- s 3: "parliamentarian means a senator or a member of the House of Representatives."
@ref MOP(S) Act 1984 s 3 'parliamentarian'
GIVEN p IS A Position
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a parliamentarian` p IF
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `former Prime Minister who is not a parliamentarian` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 3: "relevant office means: (a) an office of Minister; or (b) the office of Leader of the
-- Opposition in the Senate; or (c) the office of Leader of the Opposition in the House of
-- Representatives; or (d) the office of Deputy Leader of the Opposition in the Senate; or
-- (e) the office of Deputy Leader of the Opposition in the House of Representatives; or (f) an
-- office of leader or deputy leader, in a House of the Parliament, of a recognized political
-- party (other than an office ... referred to in any of the preceding paragraphs ...)."
@ref MOP(S) Act 1984 s 3 'relevant office'
GIVEN p IS A Position
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a relevant office` p IF
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `Prime Minister` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Minister other than the Prime Minister` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Leader of the Opposition in the Senate` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Leader of the Opposition in the House of Representatives` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Deputy Leader of the Opposition in the Senate` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Deputy Leader of the Opposition in the House of Representatives` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `leader or deputy leader in a House of a recognized political party` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN p IS A Position
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an office of Minister` p IF
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `Prime Minister` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Minister other than the Prime Minister` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 3: "office-holder means: (a) a person who holds a relevant office; or (b) a person, not
-- being a parliamentarian, who held the office of Prime Minister; or (c) a parliamentarian in
-- respect of whom a determination under section 4 is in force."
-- s 4(1): "The Prime Minister may, in writing, determine that ... the parliamentarian may employ
-- personal employees under subsection 11(3)." Whether a determination was in force is a fact.
@ref MOP(S) Act 1984 s 3 'office-holder', s 4(1)
GIVEN p IS A Position, determination IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an office-holder` p `with a section 4 determination in force` determination IF
        `is a relevant office` p
     OR (CONSIDER p
         WHEN `former Prime Minister who is not a parliamentarian` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
     OR (`is a parliamentarian` p AND determination)

§ `Members of Parliament (Staff) Act 1984 s 11 -- Employment`

-- s 11(1): "A parliamentarian may, on behalf of the Commonwealth, employ a person, under a
-- written agreement, as an electorate employee."
-- s 11(2): "A Minister may, on behalf of the Commonwealth, employ a person ... as a personal
-- employee (Ministerial)."
-- s 11(3): "An office-holder other than a Minister may, on behalf of the Commonwealth, employ a
-- person ... as a personal employee (non-Ministerial)."
-- Whether an engagement of this kind by a person in this position is employment under the Act.
@ref MOP(S) Act 1984 s 11(1)-(3)
GIVEN k IS A `MOP(S) Act employment`, p IS A Position, determination IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `employment as` k `by a person occupying` p `with a section 4 determination in force` determination `is authorised by section 11` IF
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `electorate employee` THEN `is a parliamentarian` p
    WHEN `personal employee (Ministerial)` THEN `is an office of Minister` p
    WHEN `personal employee (non-Ministerial)` THEN
            `is an office-holder` p `with a section 4 determination in force` determination
        AND (NOT `is an office of Minister` p)

-- s 3AA(1): "The employing individual, for a person employed under this Act, is the
-- parliamentarian or office-holder who, on behalf of the Commonwealth, employed the person under
-- section 11." The employing individual is whoever the caller says engaged the person; this
-- module asks only whether the engagement was one s 11 authorises.
